(193: (meta: (t: semantic) (n: 1) (term: string%20value) (def: We%20need%20to%20make%20sure%20our%20engine%20works%20as%20readonly%20or%20mutable%20as%20per%20user%20configuration%2C%20CST%2FAST%20for%20all%20popular%20programming%20languages%2C%20data%20exchange%20formats%2C%20and%20other%20popular%20formal%20languages%2C%20and%20also%20natural%20languages%20%28including%20actual%20parsing%20of%20their%20grammar%20with%20no%20semantic%20checks%2C%20meaning%20matching%20and%20logic%20correctness%20is%20out%20of%20the%20scope%20of%20this%20project%2C%20but%20grammatical%20correctness%2C%20syntax%20correctness%20and%20so%20on%20-%20should%20be%20fully%20supported%29.%0A%0AWe%20also%20should%20have%20advanced%20shared%20concepts%20space%20between%20languages%2C%20which%20should%20be%20reused%20when%20only%20matched%20exactly%2C%20so%20it%20will%20help%20to%20simplify%20automated%20translation%20between%20any%20languages%2C%20transformation%20and%20mutation%20of%20texts%2Fcode%2Fmessages%20in%20any%20language%20and%20so%20on.%0A%0ASo%20we%20need%20to%20be%20able%20to%20fully%20support%20storage%20%28presenting%20as%20links%20notation%20%28text%20based%20as%20in%20https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Flink-foundation%2Flinks-notation%29%2C%20binary%20links%20as%20in%20https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Flinksplatform%2Fdoublets-rs%20and%20https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Flinksplatform%2Fdoublets-web%29%2C%20and%20also%20Rust%20traits%2Ftypes%20representation.%0A%0Agithub.com%2Flink-assistant%2Fformal-ai%20will%20be%20our%20the%20most%20heavy%20user%2C%20so%20we%20need%20to%20make%20sure%20any%20language%20can%20be%20treated%20easily%20as%20data%2C%20and%20we%20can%20do%20any%20transformations%20and%20substitutions%20in%20style%20of%20github.com%2Flink-foundation%2Flink-cli%2C%20and%20also%20other%20traditional%20API%20adapters%2C%20like%20chaining%2C%20direct%20OOP%20methods%20and%20so%20on.%20So%20all%20the%20same%20operations%20should%20be%20possible%20to%20be%20used%20by%20all%20kinds%20of%20ways%2C%20so%20user%20can%20decide%20whatever%20he%20prefer%20best%20and%20use%20it.%20All%20of%20APIs%20styles%20should%20support%20all%20the%20same%20operations%20up%20on%20the%20languages%20described%20in%20meta-language.%0A%0AOur%20meta%20language%20should%20also%20provide%20ability%20to%20translate%20any%20other%20language%20to%20meta%20language%20and%20from%20meta%20language.%20Meaning%20all%20data%20manipulations%20should%20be%20done%20up%20on%20our%20meta%20language%2C%20but%20if%20we%20want%20to%20keep%20working%20with%20single%20language%20for%20example%20for%20javascript%20to%20javascript%20transformation%20-%20we%20just%20restrict%20ourselves%20with%20using%20only%20features%20of%20meta%20language%20that%20JavaScript%20supports%20exactly%20and%20so%20on.%0A%0AIf%20we%20do%20cross%20language%20translation%2C%20we%20need%20to%20make%20sure%20our%20API%20is%20expandable%20and%20all%20missing%20translation%20from%20meta%20language%20and%20to%20meta%20language%20are%20expandable%20and%20configurable%20by%20end%20user%2C%20so%20he%20will%20be%20able%20to%20support%20cross%20language%20rules%20based%20translation%2C%20with%20full%20freedom%20of%20configuration%2C%20so%20everything%20in%20our%20system%20should%20be%20replaceable%2C%20configurable%20and%20so%20on.%20So%20widest%20possible%20range%20of%20operations%20for%20any%20language%20via%20the%20prism%20of%20meta%20language%20will%20be%20supported.%0A%0AWe%20should%20check%20that%20nothing%20is%20defered%20or%20left%20unimplemented%20in%20our%20vision%20and%20roadmap.%20We%20should%20have%20100%25%20tests%20coverage%2C%20which%20should%20copy%20most%20of%20test%20cases%20from%20our%20competitors%20in%20each%20sector%2Fscope.%0A%0AFor%20each%20aspect%20of%20this%20task%2C%20we%20should%20create%20issues%20on%20GitHub%2C%20with%20clear%20blocked%20by%20markings%2C%20so%20we%20know%20in%20which%20order%20to%20execute%20all%20the%20task%2C%20as%20we%20the%20result%20we%20will%20combine%20all%20tasks%20in%20pull%20request%20for%20this%20specific%20task.%0A%0ASo%20all%20tasks%20should%20also%20be%20subtasks%20of%20this%20task.%20All%20tasks%20will%20be%20executed%20on%20the%20branch%20for%20this%20task%2C%20so%20everything%20will%20be%20merged%20into%20single%20big%20pull%20request.%0A%0AIf%20it%20is%20required%20it%20is%20ok%20to%20make%20architectural%20and%20breaking%20changes.%20Our%20goal%20is%20to%20have%20the%20best%20possible%20tool%20for%20exactly%20any%20possible%20task%20with%20languages.%0A%0AWe%20need%20to%20collect%20data%20related%20about%20the%20issue%20to%20this%20repository%2C%20make%20sure%20we%20compile%20that%20data%20to%20%60.%2Fdocs%2Fcase-studies%2Fissue-%7Bid%7D%60%20folder%2C%20and%20use%20it%20to%20do%20deep%20case%20study%20analysis%20%28also%20make%20sure%20to%20search%20online%20for%20additional%20facts%20and%20data%29%2C%20list%20of%20each%20and%20all%20requirements%20from%20the%20issue%2C%20and%20propose%20possible%20solutions%20and%20solution%20plans%20for%20each%20requirement%20%28we%20should%20also%20check%20known%20existing%20components%2Flibraries%2C%20that%20solve%20similar%20problem%20or%20can%20help%20in%20solutions%29.) (lang: meta-language%20structured%20data)))
